  "scene": {
    "id": "overlap-pilot4",
    "language": "All right, so how overlapping works is right now you're being defended with the ball in front of the opponent, so the opponent is defending you from their goal. You want to try to score but you can't because you're being defended and that's not a good positi- position. So what you need to do is pass it to your teammate, which is me. I'm gonna try to go around you, which is what overlapping is. I'm gonna try to go around you to go to a better position where you could then pass the ball to me, and then I could either score or pass it back to you. Let's see how this works. [0][1](scuffling noises)[2] [3]Okay, so now I have the ball and I'm in a better position than you were to score the goal. So then since the opponent is now over here and I have a clear path to the goal, then it is better for me to score. So let's do it. (scuffling noises)[4] And that is why overlapping is a useful advantage for us to switch positions and switch who has the ball so that we can make the goal.",
